<title>MEXICO: Mexico auto production, exports rise.</title>
<headline>Mexico auto production, exports rise.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican auto production for the first 10 months of the year was 1,041,484 units, a rise of 276,943 compared with the same period last year, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Production for export during the January-October period was 831,111, up 30.2 percent compared with the first 10 months of last year.  </p>
<p>Average vehicle sales during the first 10 months of the year were 24,156 units, still shy of 1994 pre-devaluation levels of 48,661, the association said.</p>
<p>The following table compares production and sales data for cars and trucks and buses during the relevant periods. Last year's figures are either a number or a percentage change.</p>
<p>				    JAN-OCT 96	     JAN-OCT 95</p>
<p>    TOTAL PRODUCTION	   1,041,484		+36.2 pct</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 210,373		+66.4 pct</p>
<p>		autos		     n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>		trucks and buses	n.a.		     n.a.</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   831,111		+30.2 pct</p>
<p>		autos		  554,656		+10.7 pct</p>
<p>		trucks and buses   276,455		 +102 pct</p>
<p>    TOTAL SALES		  1,076,003		  763,632</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 245,927		  133,605</p>
<p>	   EXPORT SALES	    830,076		  630,027</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC RETAIL SALES 240,266		  182,381</p>
<p>		autos		  145,112		  105,133</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    95,154		   67,348</p>
<p>	     -- Mexico City newsroom,</p>
